 the art of crochet.\nIn this beginner-friendly workshop with Dear Homie Cr
 ochet\, we’ll walk through the fundamentals together - no experience nee
 ded\, just good vibes and a willingness to try something new.\nYou’ll le
 arn up to 2–3 foundational stitches (time permitting)\, plus all the lit
 tle things that make a big difference (like how to hold your hook comforta
 bly\, read yarn labels\, and actually understand what you’re doing … n
 ot just copy it).\nThis is a skills-based class designed to set you up wit
 h a strong foundation\, so you can confidently keep going on your own (and
  maybe get a little obsessed with it)\nWhether you’re coming solo or wit
 h a friend\, expect a relaxed\, supportive environment where you can learn
 \, ask questions\, and make something with your hands.\nAGE APPROPRIATENES
 S:\n14+\nLEVEL:\nBeginner: no previous experience required\nMATERIALS PROV
 IDED/ TAKE HOME\nCrochet hook\nStitch markers\nPractice yarn to take home\
 nPrint instruction manual
