 g life in the (human-dominated) celebrity spotlight. But along the way\, D
 on will be confronted with some harsh truths about himself\, chickenkind a
 nd humankind.\n"This show where a woman who plays a chicken who thinks he'
 s an Irishman is unlike anything you've ever seen." — Playbill\nThis pla
 y is part of the Canada Ireland Foundation’s Bealtaine Theatre Festival\
 , which brings the best of Irish Theatre to Toronto. Learn more: https://w
 ww.canadairelandfoundation.com/explore/bealtaine-theatre-festival-2026/\nO
 n Stage May 21-24\, 2025\nSingle tickets starting at just $55 (incl. tax &
  fees)\nChicken\nBy Sunday's Child Theatre\nCo-written by Eva O’Connor a
 nd Hildegard Ryan\nDirected by Hildegard Ryan\nFeaturing Eva O’Connor
LOCATION:Corleck
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/chicken-toronto/
