  than 200 youth volunteers and 100\,000 participants from local families\,
  and tourists from the wider area in the world.\n\n500 artists\, musicians
 \, heritage performers\, and authors\, from Cambodian\, Chinese\, Indian\,
  Japanese\, Korean\, Malaysian\, Philippines\, Sri- Lankan\, Thai\, and ma
 ny other communities have been invited to participate and present multicul
 tural performing arts\, visual arts\, digital arts\, and publishes.\n\nDis
 cover Asian cultures via more than 100 programs on the outdoor stage in th
 ree days (a total of 16 hours) for demonstrative traditional and contempor
 ary music\, art workshops\, book fairs\, movies\, dance\, fashion shows\, 
 and much more performances\, and art exhibitions in diversities\n\nAlso en
 joy outdoor Asian Delicious in three days (a total of 36 hours) via tradit
 ional food vendors\, the most popular destiny for families and tourists
