BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Black Sheep Comedy @ Rorschach Brewing Co. Featuring KENNY ROBINSO
 N
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T213000
UID:blogto-235137@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/17/original_image1da1c555-7953-4e16-bab6-01a680472e
 38.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a night of incredible comedy and craft beer! The F
 abulous Kenny Robinson headlines and a complimentary beverage is provided.
 \nIt's Black Sheep Comedy's last pro stand up show of the season\, and we'
 re wrapping up with a bang! Canadian comedy legend KENNY ROBINSON headline
 s this hilarious lineup\, including Jeremy Dobski\, Karlie Laverty\, Dhama
  & Dre Pavez.\nTickets are just $20 in advance or $25 at the door (if avai
 lable) and includes a 12oz beer or pop.\nNot quite convinced yet? Check ou
 t Kenny Robinson's bio!\nKENNY ROBINSON\n"The Fabulous Kenny Robinson" is 
 a living legend on the Canadian Comedy scene.\nHis irreverent\, socially c
 onscience\, intelligent\, opinionated and profane style of comedy has made
  him a fixture and favourite with comedy clubs\, festivals\, swingers conv
 entions\, radio\, and television audiences for 3 decades.\nThe Winnipeg bo
 rn\, Chicago bred Robinson has hosted The Gemini Awards and was twice nomi
 nated for his writing and performance in his ground breaking one hour spec
 ial "Thick and Thin" on the CBC. Kenny has earned accolades as the creator
 \, writer\, producer and host of the edgy late night series" After Hours w
 ith Kenny Robinson" on The Comedy Network.\nHis episode of the CBC's Comic
 s has been referred by the Toronto Star as "One of the few episodes that s
 till stand with the test of time."\nFor 2 years he was one of the co hosts
  of "The Morning Rush" on Flow 93.5fm\, Canada's first black owned hip hop
  radio station.\nAs an actor Kenny has appeared in such films as "Third Mi
 racle" with Ed Harris\, "Down To Earth" with Chris Rock\, Clement Virgo's 
 "Love comes Down"\, and David Sutherland's "Love\, Sex\, and Eating the Bo
 nes." Robinson has appeared on the CBC's "Royal Canadian Air Farce"\, Show
 time's "Soul Food"\, and has a wide fan base from his re-occurring roles a
 s "Jelly Bean" on PAX series "Doc"\, starring Billy Ray Cyrus\, and as "Mi
 ckey" on the teen fave "Radio Free Roscoe" on the "Noggin" Network.\nWheth
 er the audience looks for his cutting observational perspectives\, politic
 al\, sexual or what comes up at the moment\, Kenny's professional attitude
  and love for comedy will always deliver!
LOCATION:Rorschach Brewing
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/black-sheep-comedy-rorschach-brewing-co-
 featuring-kenny-robinson-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blossom Sound Bath
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T214500
UID:blogto-234246@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/27/original_imaged0f76b26-5268-4398-be09-73217fa9c1
 ce.jpg
DESCRIPTION:As the earth unfurls and the resonance of birdsong fills the a
 ir\, we gather to greet the season of becoming\, as new life emerges withi
 n and around us. Join certified sound therapy practitioner\, song-carrier\
 , and yoga & meditation guide Michaela Bekenn for an immersive sound journ
 ey to refresh the body\, revitalize the mind\, and soften the heart.\nBe h
 eld in the live vibrations of crystal singing bowls\, drum\, voice and mor
 e - each reflecting the music of the earth. These frequencies may invite n
 ourishing processes to take place such as: regulating the nervous system\,
  dissolving tension\, slowing the brainwaves\, and cultivating deep cellul
 ar rest.\nThere is nothing expected of you - simply arrive as you are and 
 explore the practice of full-body listening. It has been said\, that sound
  is one of our 'most ancient technologies of belonging\,' with potential t
 o guide us toward deeper states of consciousness\, relaxation\, and interc
 onnection. The session begins with gentle seated movement and deep breath\
 , to invite a soft landing. No prior experience with meditation or sound t
 herapy is necessary. Wear what makes you feel most comfortable.\nOptional:
  bring a small item that connects you to the energy of the earth\, to be t
 emporarily added to our collective centerpiece\, as we cultivate reverence
  and beauty together. Please bring your item home at the end.
LOCATION:Breathe Yoga Studio
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/blossom-sound-bath-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
