BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dance Division 012 / May 22 / Special Birthday Edition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T050000
UID:blogto-234622@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/05/original_imagef01462c0-7aa9-4245-9fdc-2bccd026da
 2e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:May 22nd\, join us for in celebrating co-founder Rami Aburob's
  birthday! With resident and co-founder Nour featuring guest DJs Esther Be
 noit\, Coach Rich + PRSIS10S and North Haus.\nDance Division returns for i
 ts 12th instalment\, celebrating underground sounds and diverse selectors\
 , from rising DJs to seasoned veterans. All genders\, queer artists\, and 
 allies come together with one goal: to make you dance.\nSet Times:\nNorth 
 Haus: 10-11\nEsther Benoit: 11-12\nRami Aburob: 12-2\nNour: 2-3\nCoach Ric
 h + PRSIST10S: 3 to close\nVJ Prabin will be tantalizing our senses with h
 is sick visuals as per usual!\nYour artists:\nRami Abourob is a genre-blen
 ding DJ known for his groovy\, ground-shaking sets that fuse tech house wi
 th disco\, hip hop\, and Middle Eastern samples. He improvises his sets ma
 inly relying on reading the crowd\, and selecting tracks that take them on
  a journey.\nsoundcloud.com/rami-abu-rob\nESTHER BENOIT (DJ/producer)\, ma
 de her debut in 2010 in Montreal\, let her flair for the dramatic mark the
  local scene\, and has been spinning regularly since. Esther spent her for
 mative years in the Montreal scene and later moved to Toronto where she fu
 rther developed her style. She mixes a combination of minimal\, deep tech\
 , and techno: ranging from light\, funky\, and playful to shamelessly deep
  and dirty.\nCurrently based in Toronto\, Esther has played at countless l
 ocal venues and parties such as Vertigo Afterhours and Promise Cherry Beac
 h\, and has travelled to perform in other cities like NYC\, Halifax\, and 
 more. She’s also a Techno.FM resident\, where she broadcasts the long-ru
 nning weekly show\, Rebel Mix.\nShe's released on the labels Poker Flat Re
 cordings and Natura Viva Music\, including her remix of Joyce Muniz's trac
 k What's Your Name ft Demetrius.\nhttps://soundcloud.com/estherbenoit\nNOU
 R is a DJ\, dancer\, and co-founder of Dance Division\, known for her genr
 e-blending sets\, global influences\, and seamless transitions. Inspired b
 y her Beirut roots and travels\, she curates intentional\, high-energy jou
 rneys that keep dance floors moving. She’s played multiple festivals thi
 s summer of 2025 including Camp Wiggle\, Camp Summerdaze\, Phantom and the
  Orphan Burn. A Wiggle Room DJ first\, but has also shared music in multip
 le venues for various dancers and music lovers.\nsoundcloud.com/nour-bawab
 \nCOACH RICH Born-and-raised in Parkdale\, Toronto\, Coach Rich loves to m
 eld genres together to create a unique\, bouncy\, eclectic vibe on the dan
 cefloor. He longs for times remembered\, times that are present\, in the m
 oment. From melodic sunset vibes on the beach\, to dancing with your horns
  out to the clang of industrial sounds\, his message is one of unity\, one
  of safety\, and unjudged freedom. Bounce\, sweat\, dance\; move as you ar
 e\, all are welcome.\nhttps://soundcloud.com/coachrichcuts\nP R S I S 1 0 
 S Born & raised in Toronto\, Kevin has a knack for creating a musical atmo
 sphere that violates all expectations. He quickly developed a passion for 
 dark\, moody & raw sounds. Running the up and coming Isocutscrew his story
  has just begun!\nhttps://www.instagram.com/prsis10s/\nNORTH HAUS DJ sets
  deliver tension and release\, with elements of House and Techno. Engineer
 ed for physical immersion\, his sound is designed to be felt in the chest 
 - creating a room where people can shed their worries and lose themselves 
 in the movement of the room. A rising force in the Toronto club scene\, No
 rth Haus has transitioned years of honing his craft into live presence\, k
 nown for rhythms that dominate the crowd."\nThe name North Haus is a part 
 of his dual identity – born in the Canadian North with deep German roots
 . It Includes his heritage with a lifelong passion for electronic music.\n
 https://soundcloud.com/user-570790295\nVJ Prabin is a visual artist who ex
 plores how sound can look in three dimensions. His path started behind a d
 rumkit\; however\, after an accident necessitated a break from drumming\, 
 he began focusing on how to move light and graphics with the same rhythm h
 e once found in music. This transition led him to a space where his intere
 sts in photography\, music\, and technology finally aligned.\nOver the las
 t decade\, he has developed a practice centered on 3D modeling\, 2D/3D ani
 mation\, projection mapping\, and live VJing\, aiming to create art that p
 eople can truly step inside. He builds his own 3D structures and brings th
 em to life through digital graphics and immersive projections. Having perf
 ormed at events across Nepal and Canada since 2013\, Prabin focuses on the
  natural sync between visuals and the music's pulse.\nFor him\, the goal i
 sn't just to put on a show\, but to help create those moments where the au
 dience can lose themselves in the harmony of sight and sound.\nOur venue @
 wiggleroomtoronto is the #HomeOfBouncyBeats\, home to a strong underground
  community and the heart of the scene.\nDiscounted tickets above are limit
 ed. Follow for updates and announcements at DanceDivision.to.\nYour hosts 
 for the night:\n@nour_toronto\, @djaburob\, and @esbeesy.\n#DANCEDANCEDANC
 E\nBehave. You know what to do and not to do.
LOCATION:Wiggle Room
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/dance-division-012-may-22-special-birthd
 ay-edition-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
