BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dave Gunning - Healing Garden Fundraiser
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T220000
UID:blogto-235309@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/20/original_image93f801ca-ee6e-4895-8c7d-21abc83f35
 94.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Close the 28th season with us at Acoustic Harvest.\nJoin us on
  Saturday\, May 23 for our final concert of the season\, a special evening
  with acclaimed Nova Scotia singer-songwriter Dave Gunning\, presented as 
 a fundraiser in support of the Healing Garden project to create gardens of
  solace in hospital settings for patients undergoing the rigours of cancer
 .\nAcoustic Harvest has always been more than a concert series. It is a pl
 ace to hear outstanding artists\, but also a place to meet friends\, share
  conversation\, and feel part of a warm musical community. This season-clo
 sing show is a chance to gather one more time before summer.\nDave Gunning
  is one of Canada’s most respected folk singer-songwriters. A multiple E
 ast Coast Music Award and Canadian Folk Music Award winner\, he is known f
 or his warm stage presence\, sharp wit\, heartfelt storytelling\, and song
 s that honour everyday people and hard truths.\nThe evening opens with Tai
 vi & Garth\, setting the tone for a night of music\, friendship\, and comm
 unity.\nCome for the songs. Come for the cause. Come to close the season w
 ith us.\nOpening Set: Taivi & Garth\nDave Gunning: Healing Garden Fundrais
 er\nFinal Acoustic Harvest concert of the season
LOCATION:Acoustic Harvest
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/dave-gunning-healing-garden-fundraiser-t
 oronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DesignTO Tours: Montague House
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T120000
UID:blogto-234113@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/23/original_image4b84e9ac-eca8-452c-89ef-f38c9cf2d1
 d4.jpg
DESCRIPTION:May 23\, 2026 | 10:30am – 12:00pm\nWychwood Park\, Toronto\n
 Tickets: $100\nSupport DesignTO’s charitable programming while gaining r
 are access to a remarkable private residence in Toronto’s Wychwood Park 
 neighbourhood. The Montague House tour is a special fundraising event\, wi
 th proceeds directly supporting DesignTO’s year-round work advancing des
 ign and creativity in Canada. A charitable tax receipt will be issued for 
 the allowable portion of each ticket.\nThis one-of-a-kind experience offer
 s access to the home of collector Dr. Kenneth Montague and artist and educ
 ator Sarah Aranha. Originally designed in 1919 by Arts and Crafts architec
 t Eden Smith\, the house has been carefully restored and expanded by Studi
 o for Contemporary Architecture to accommodate a growing family and an ext
 ensive collection of art\, objects\, and design.\nSpanning 5\,000 square f
 eet across three levels\, the home is conceived as a setting for living wi
 th art. Works from the renowned Wedge Collection are integrated throughout
 \, reflecting Montague’s commitment to championing Black artists and fos
 tering dialogue through his work with Wedge Curatorial Projects. Thoughtfu
 l architectural interventions create layered sightlines and moments of pau
 se\, framing the collection within contemporary living spaces.\nThe tour w
 ill be led by the homeowners\, architect Tura Cousins Wilson\, and DesignT
 O Artistic Director Deborah Wang\, offering unique insight into the design
  process\, the evolution of the home\, and the role of collecting in shapi
 ng space.\nAttendees may request a certificate for 1 hour of structured co
 ntinuing education following the tour. Guests will also receive a complime
 ntary gift from Aesop.\nSpace is limited. Advance registration required.
LOCATION:Montague House
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/designto-tours-montague-house-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
