BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Siksikakowan: The Blackfoot Man
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T205000
UID:blogto-233631@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_image99b3161f-1877-4c97-8f98-37b8771c36
 4d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:“Growing up in Siksika\, masculinity was all around me but w
 as unclear. Now\, using my lens\, I seek to find clarity.” Grounded on t
 he land that has provided for his ancestors since time immemorial\, filmma
 ker Sinakson Trevor Solway\, addresses the past by looking forward with ge
 nerations of Blackfoot men who are rebuilding culture and community in the
 ir work and recreation. Each of them has a unique journey and story to sha
 re about the challenges they face. Important introspective questions frame
  thoughtful observations about what modern masculinity does and doesn’t 
 look like\, especially for those who have been stigmatized and misundersto
 od. Roping cattle\, singing\, playing hockey and participating in Ceremony
  all play distinct yet important roles in how these men support each other
 . Artists\, athletes\, ranchers and many others share vulnerable and authe
 ntic reflections on their lives that culminate in an exceptional vérité 
 portrait of kinship and resilience for these Siksika sons\, fathers\, husb
 ands and brothers. Alexander Rogalski\, Hot Docs\nJoin director Trevor Sol
 way for a special post-screening discussion on May 23.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/siksikakowan-the-blackfoot-man-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonic Sancocho Edicion Como la Flor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T230000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T040000
UID:blogto-235249@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/20/original_imagefbc7bbe8-6672-4339-993c-eafd69f0e5
 48.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Spring has sprung! Join us at Drom Taberna with performances b
 y Marta Elena and her band\, and local DJ General Eclectic!\nIt's time to 
 bloom...como la flor\, con Marta Elena y Sonic Sancocho!\nJoin Sonic Sanco
 cho in welcoming the spring season for the first of three 2026 marquee eve
 nts at Drom Taberna!\nHeadlining the night is the unparalleled Marta Elena
 . Accompanied by her incredible band\, the Toronto-based Cuban-Canadian so
 ngstress will deliver classics\, contemporaries and music from her new alb
 um\, Por Amor\, out now on Lulaworld Records - her most mature and emotion
 ally resonant work to date. Known for her expressive voice and dynamic sta
 ge presence\, Marta Elena moves effortlessly between powerful\, rhythm-dri
 ven performance and intimate storytelling. Her music is deeply personal\, 
 often inspired by everyday life\, cultural memory\, and the communities th
 at shape her artistic journey.\nA Toronto legend\, we are excited to welco
 me DJ General Eclectic as our guest DJ. From cumbia to chutney\, forro to 
 funk\, soul to soukous...His ability to rock a party has kept him in the c
 ompany of some of the best DJs from around the globe\, while at home he’
 s built a longstanding reputation for community building events and creati
 ve projects that have made a lasting mark on the city’s cultural landsca
 pe.\nAs always\, Founders\, Juana Go-gó and olasconola will share a bold 
 blend of music to welcome you to the party.\nComplimentary cup of Sancocho
  at midnight for ticket holders - please note: first come\, first served.\
 nWhat is Sancocho? Learn more about the history here.\nAdvance Eventbrite 
 ticket holders must check in to the venue by 11 pm.\nDate: Saturday\, May 
 23\, 2026\nDoors: 10:30 pm\nMusic: 11:00 pm - 4:00 am\nLocation: DROM Tabe
 rna\, Queen Street West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada\nAbout Sonic Sancocho:The 
 spice of life in sound\, shared with community. Much like ingredients in a
  universal dish - a big pot of soup - here\, platters of sound are spun an
 d served with warm welcome. Musical ingredients from around the world\, fr
 om a local perspective\, for all to share and enjoy. Founded by selectress
 es olasconola & Juana Go-Go in Toronto\, Canada\, Sonic Sancocho is a comm
 unity gathering of music and food - two things that nourish heart and soul
 .They bring forth the B Sides and the beloved of Latin music\, with sounds
  from around the world\, to your venue through all-vinyl DJ sets and dynam
 ic live performances. Sancocho is where all of the ingredients come togeth
 er and are shared amongst one another - from the starches to the spices an
 d everything in between. We turn up the heat to bring it to a boil\, comin
 g together to enjoy a moment of connection through a serving of soup\, wit
 hin layers of sound\, endless movement and fun.\nTune in to the radio show
 \, hosted & produced by Juana Go-gó - Sundays at 2:00 pm ET on CIUT 89.5 
 FM!\nAbout Marta Elena:\nMarta Elena is a Cuban-Canadian singer\, composer
 \, and bandleader based in Toronto\, whose work bridges Afro-Cuban traditi
 ons with contemporary Latin sounds. Trained in Havana and shaped by a care
 er that includes touring internationally with the legendary all-female orc
 hestra Anacaona\, she has developed a distinctive voice rooted in traditio
 n yet open to global influences.\nHer debut album\, De La Habana a Toronto
 \, established her as a compelling presence in Canada’s Latin music scen
 e\, blending Cuban heritage with the multicultural energy of her adopted c
 ity. With her latest release\, Por Amor (2026)\, Marta Elena delivers her 
 most mature and emotionally resonant work to date.\nDeeply grounded in Afr
 o-Latin music\, Por Amor expands her sound through elements of salsa\, bol
 ero\, changüí\, rumba\, and touches of funk—reflecting both tradition 
 and evolution. The album\, produced in collaboration with acclaimed pianis
 t and arranger Hilario Durán\, highlights her strengths as both a vocalis
 t and songwriter\, featuring a majority of original compositions alongside
  carefully selected Latin American classics.\nWith Por Amor\, she continue
 s to position herself as a leading voice in Canada’s global music landsc
 ape—an artist who honors her roots while pushing Latin music forward wit
 h authenticity and vision.\nAbout DJ General Eclectic:\nFor nearly 3 decad
 es DJ General Eclectic has been seamlessly blending his way across all gen
 res of music\, from cumbia to chutney\, forro to funk\, soul to soukous...
 His ability to rock a party has kept him in the company of some of the bes
 t DJs from around the globe\, while at home he’s built a longstanding re
 putation for community building events and creative projects that have mad
 e a lasting mark on the city’s cultural landscape.
LOCATION:Drom Taberna
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/sonic-sancocho-edicion-como-la-flor-toro
 nto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
