BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alex Harding\, Detroit - An Afternoon For Ornette and Coltrane
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T160000
UID:blogto-235117@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/16/original_imagef8bd2753-5861-4d27-91d6-0882483daf
 bf.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Alex Harding was born in Detroit\, Michigan. At the age of six
 \, Alex knew what he wanted to do in his lifetime: to be a musician. He st
 arted to pursue his dream. Alex started on Drums & a few years later after
  hearing Grover Washington Jr on the radio playing Mr. Magic Alex switched
  to the tenor sax. Mr. Harding took band classes in elementary\, middle sc
 hool & high school\, entering musical competitions and shows.\nAlex Hardin
 g studied music in his early years with Yusef Lateef\, Beans Bows and Herb
 ie Williams\, and played with Wynton Marsalis and Donald Byrd while still 
 in high school. Alex went on to win music scholarships to the University o
 f Massachusetts and the Aspen School of Music. Alex’s first European eng
 agement in 1990 was in Porgy and Bess. A year later\, he went to Mexico to
  the Arts and Music Festival with percussionist Francisco Mora.He has work
 ed with Muhal Richard Abrams\, Craig Harris\, Lester Bowie\, Frank Lacey\,
  Oliver Lake and David Murray’s Big Band.\nIn 1996\, Alex joined Hamiet 
 Bluiett’s Baritone Group and appeared with the Mingus Big Band\, Jayne C
 ortez Firespitters and Lester Bowie’s Hip-Hop Philharmonic. He recorded 
 with Greg Osby\, Frank Lowe\, David Lee Roth and Rodney Whittaker. The fol
 lowing year\, Alex recorded At Doctor King’s Table with the Julius Hemph
 ill Sextet\, a CD with Hamiet Bluiett’s Baritone Group\, and he made his
  debut with the Sun Ra Arkestra under Marshall Allen’s leadership. In 19
 98\, Alex was part of the Sun Ra All-Star Project that premiered at the No
 rth Sea Jazz Festival and the Montreux-Detroit Jazz Festival. More recentl
 y Alex has performed with the Roy Hargrove Big Band and with Aretha Frankl
 in.Alex Harding has recorded for CIMP label and since 2008 he has performe
 d on Broadway and toured with the (3) Tony Award winning show FELA !!!!\nA
  powerful and innovative saxophonist\, Alex Harding has a unique and conte
 mporary baritone sound. The sincerity of his musical _expression and the d
 ynamism of his performance reaches out and touches the human spirit and so
 ul.\nSunday May 24\, 2026\n1:30-4pm in CONTXT\n$25adv | $35 door
LOCATION:CONTXT by Trane
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/alex-harding-detroit-an-afternoon-for-or
 nette-and-coltrane-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
