DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T213000
UID:blogto-235144@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/18/original_image54bd20bd-9090-453e-b31b-ddb00c493d
 c7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Opening Night of Annual Jewish Music Week - We welcome back Sc
 hmaltz and Pepper!\nSchmaltz and Pepper have been blazing a trail\, settin
 g records\, and changing the sound of klezmer and Yiddish  swing as we kno
 w it.\nWith  their combined talents and experience in countless musical ge
 nres\, these stellar musicians are redefining the traditional boundaries o
 f Jewish music\, blending classical mastery with innovative\, soulful arra
 ngements.\nAn unforgettable musical experience from a major force in the g
 lobal music scene!\nFeaturing: Eric Abramovitz\, principal clarinetist of 
 the Toronto Symphony.\nDrew Jurecka\, Grammy winner\, multi-instrumentalis
 t and arranger.\nRebekah Wolkstein\, founder and leader of the Payadora Ta
 ngo Ensemble\, virtuosic violinist\, vocalist and composer.\nMichael Herri
 ng\, JUNO Award- nominated bassist\nJeremy Ledbetter\, JUNO Award-winning 
 pianist.\nwww.schmaltzandpepper.com\n﻿Visit www.jewishmusicweek.com for 
 tickets -  $25/$45/$75
LOCATION:Leah Posluns Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/annual-jewish-music-week-presents-schmal
 tz-and-pepper-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Paint Your Pet Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T130000
UID:blogto-234015@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/22/original_image90bbed9d-2feb-4c2b-bda6-05e407af46
 10.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Create a heartfelt keepsake at the Paint Your Pet Experience a
 t Artbox Studio & Gallery. In this guided workshop\, you’ll turn your fu
 r baby into a personalized work of art.\nBefore the event\, simply send us
  a clear photo of your pet. We’ll have it pre-printed and ready for you 
 to trace onto your canvas\, making it easy to get started. Our instructor 
