BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:FASHION ART TORONTO - The SHOW Room at The Hudson's Bay
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T220000
UID:blogto-234616@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/05/original_image5ee17df5-7e43-4232-8a34-a21b743ae5
 36.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Fashion Art Toronto officially kicks off its Spring/Summer 202
 6 Fashion Week with a landmark takeover of the former Hudson’s Bay / Sak
 s Fifth Avenue flagship\, transforming the iconic third floor into THE (SH
 OW) ROOM — a large-scale luxury retail takeover and cultural marketplace
  featuring 100+ Canadian brands and fashion institutions.\nAccessible duri
 ng the day (12PM - 10PM) through registration through the Fashion Art Toro
 nto website)\, the activation reimagines the future of retail through imme
 rsive brand storytelling\, installations\, and direct-to-consumer experien
 ces\, opening a historically exclusive space to the wider community.\nThe 
 evening continues with runway presentations by Charles Lu and L’Uomo Str
 ano. Charles Lu delivers a two-part experience — a live behind-the-scene
 s fashion performance followed by a retrospective runway show spanning his
  career. L’Uomo Strano will present a powerful collection responding to 
 anti-trans discrimination\, using fashion as a platform for visibility and
  resistance.\nABOUT FASHION WEEK SS26\nRunning May 25–31\, 2026\, Fashio
 n Art Toronto brings together 50+ designers\, artists\, and brands through
  a city-wide program of runway shows\, immersive offsite experiences\, exh
 ibitions\, retail marketplaces\, and free public activations.\nThis season
  launches the theme Toronto\, Show Yourself — a bold call for visibility
 \, confidence\, and pride across the city’s fashion community.\nRetail A
 ccess: 12PM-10pm (retail)\nShowtimes: 6 p.m. and 10 p.m.\nCost: Ticketed /
   retail access is by registration only
LOCATION:Hudson’s Bay – CF Toronto Eaton Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/fashion-art-toronto-the-show-room-at-the
 -hudsons-bay-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fiddler on the Roof in Yiddish
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T140000
UID:blogto-230386@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/02/05/original_image44475e1c-ce78-463d-bb4f-82de0e1543
 8e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:One of the most electrifying theatrical events of the last dec
 ade is finally coming to Canada. The internationally celebrated revival of
  The National Yiddish Theatre Folksbiene production of Fiddler on the Roof
  in Yiddish with English subtitles arrives at Toronto’s historic Elgin T
 heatre from May 25 to June 7\, 2026. Presented by the Harold Green Jewish 
 Theatre Company (HGJTC)\, this landmark production is directed by the lege
 ndary Tony and Academy Award winner\, Joel Grey. The show runs for a limit
 ed engagement from May 25 to June 7\, 2026. Tickets range from $36 - $18
 0 (additional fees may apply) and are on sale now via Ticketmaster. Perfor
 med entirely in its original language with English and Russian subti
 tles\, this landmark production has been described as a “revelation”
  for returning one of Broadway’s most beloved musicals back to its cul
 tural roots in a powerfully authentic theatrical event.  This landmark p
 roduction brings one of Broadway’s most beloved musicals back to its cul
 tural roots in a powerfully authentic theatrical event. In an increasingly
  fragmented world\, this story stands as a powerful unifying force - c
 ultivating empathy\, deepening cultural understanding\, and giving voice t
 o the wisdom passed from parent to child amid constant change.  Followin
 g widespread acclaim in New York City\, Fiddler on the Roof in Yiddish mak
 es its Canadian debut this Spring.
LOCATION:The Elgin Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/fiddler-on-the-roof-in-yiddish-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
