BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fashion Art Toronto Open Air @ The Historic Distillery District Ru
 nway
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T223000
UID:blogto-234618@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/05/original_image9e37d9c1-00d9-405c-9ab0-0282b89612
 25.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Fashion Week runway programming continues at the Historic Dist
 illery District as Fashion Art Toronto brings its Open Air series to one o
 f the city’s most iconic cultural hubs. A dynamic lineup of outdoor runw
 ay presentations features Indigenous designers Ayimach Horizons and Wabano
 onkwe\, alongside the Lignes de Fuite (LDF) showcase spotlighting emerging
  French-Canadian talent.\nHighlights include Ayimach Horizons\, presenting
  a multidisciplinary collection exploring Indigenous futurism\, land\, and
  light through interconnected colour worlds\, and Wabanoonkwe’s Nocturna
 l Rose — a couture collection rooted in Anishinaabe storytelling\, featu
 ring sculptural\, beadwork-inspired florals.\nThe day is further energized
  by performances from the Tkoronto Music Festival\, including Sara Kae and
  Logan Staats\, alongside legendary DJ Blackcat\, vogueing performances\, 
 and more.\nABOUT FASHION WEEK SS26\nRunning May 25–31\, 2026\, Fashion A
 rt Toronto brings together 50+ designers\, artists\, and brands through a 
 city-wide program of runway shows\, immersive offsite experiences\, exhibi
 tions\, retail marketplaces\, and free public activations.\nThis season la
 unches the theme Toronto\, Show Yourself — a bold call for visibility\, 
 confidence\, and pride across the city’s fashion community.\nCost: Free\
 , ticketed seating.
LOCATION:The Historic Distillery District
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/fashion-art-toronto-open-air-the-histori
 c-distillery-district-runway-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
