BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Preparing for CMMC and CPCSC: What Defense Suppliers Need to Know
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T170000
UID:blogto-235054@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/14/original_image51730e20-3aed-48fa-8cdc-c6b2610630
 dc.jpg
DESCRIPTION:​​Canadian and U.S. defense contractors are facing a new c
 ompliance reality: CMMC in the United States and CPCSC in Canada. For smal
 l and mid-sized suppliers\, the challenge is not just understanding the fr
 ameworks\, but choosing an implementation approach that fits their busines
 s\, customer base\, and budget.\nThis interactive workshop will help Ontar
 io-based defense contractors\, subcontractors\, and technology suppliers c
 ompare CMMC and CPCSC\, understand where the frameworks overlap\, and expl
 ore practical implementation options for smaller teams. Sponsored by Cyber
 Care Pro and PreVeil the session will show how organizations can reduce co
 mplexity\, protect controlled information\, and build a compliance roadmap
  that supports both Canadian and cross-border opportunities.\nParticipants
  will leave with:\n1. A clear comparison of CMMC and CPCSC requirements.\n
 2. A framework for deciding whether to self-assess\, outsource\, or hybrid
 ize compliance work.\n3. Practical implementation options for identity\, d
 evice\, document\, and email protection.\n4. Guidance on how to align cybe
 rsecurity controls with defense contracting goals.\n5. A better understand
 ing of funding and support options for Ontario-based companies pursuing ce
 rtification.
LOCATION:Invest Ontario
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/preparing-for-cmmc-and-cpcsc-what-defens
 e-suppliers-need-to-know-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Primary Trust
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T210500
UID:blogto-234903@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/11/original_imageb9d99022-81ad-4f5f-bd6a-ca1e069f8b
 61.jpg
DESCRIPTION:For years\, Kenneth has found solace in the mundane routine of
  his daily life—days spent working at a local bookshop\, evenings spent 
 nursing a single mai tai at his favorite bar.\nBut when the shop closes an
 d he suddenly finds himself without a job\, his carefully ordered world is
  upended. With nothing left to anchor him\, Kenneth must step beyond the q
 uiet life he’s built and confront the fears\, dreams\, and unspoken grie
 f that have kept him at a standstill.\nWith warmth and delicate humor\, Eb
 oni Booth (Paris at the Atlantic Theater Company) crafts an affirming and 
 tender portrait of a man standing at the brink of profound change.\nWinner
  of the 2024 Pulitzer Prize for Drama\, Primary Trust is a poignant medita
 tion on connection and the courage it takes to transform your life.\n🎟 
 Tickets: https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1011
LOCATION:Crow's Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/primary-trust-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
