BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gallery Tour: Allegra Charleston on Glorious Catastrophe
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T193000
UID:blogto-234945@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/12/original_imagee9a8fc2a-dbb3-4b6b-9ef5-80d0d42bdd
 2c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a delightfully irreverent Exhibition Walkthrough o
 f Glorious Catastrophe | Gillian Iles with Susie Burpee's charmingly eccen
 tric persona\, Allegra Charleston\, who dares to laugh in the face of conv
 ention.\nCharleston's art commentary challenges the art world's seriousnes
 s with sharp wit\, playful antics\, and a flair for the absurd. Don't miss
  the chance to tour this exhibition with an "art critic" who believes in a
 pproaching art with a good\, old-fashioned belly laugh.\n-\nTraversing bot
 h dance and theatre\, Susie Burpee is a multi-faceted artist and award-win
 ning performer based in Toronto/Tkaronto. Known for her character-driven c
 horeographic works\, Susie has received Dora Mavor Moore Awards for Outsta
 nding Choreography and Performance\, and she is a recipient of the K.M. Hu
 nter Artist Award for Dance.\nSusie studied Character and Bouffon with Phi
 lippe Gaulier\, where her alter ego and lifelong companion Allegra Charles
 ton was born. Susie and Allegra have been revelling in the Canadian art wo
 rld for many years\, delivering thought-provoking performances in service 
 of levity\, gravity and empathy.\nSusie holds an MA in Drama\, Theatre\, a
 nd Performance Studies from the The University of Toronto and teaches regu
 larly in post-secondary dance programs. She is now Executive Director of B
 alancing Act\, a national initiative to support parents and caregivers in 
 the performing arts. Susie is a mother\, and her work in the arts is wholl
 y informed by maternity and care-centred practices.
LOCATION:Koffler Gallery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/gallery-tour-allegra-charleston-on-glori
 ous-catastrophe-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
