 f7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:I'm reaching out to share the press documents for HERAE\, a To
 ronto-based maximalist jewelry brand I launched this year.\nMy name is Ije
 oma. I'm a 4th-generation jeweler and I just launched HERAE\, a maximalist
  jewelry brand based in Toronto. My great-grandmother made Jewelry in Nige
 ria\, my grandmother made jewelry pieces through Catholic churches and my 
 mother distributed jewelry across Nigeria. gold. I packed my bags\, moved 
 to Canada three years ago\, and now building HERAE from scratch.\nHERAE ex
 ists because bold\, durable\, statement accessible jewelry was missing fro
 m this market. The debut collection\, The 4th\, is inspired by the Nigeria
 n owambe and the traditional scarves (gele/Ichafu)\, and it's made for wom
 en of every background who wear jewelry as a statement\, not an afterthoug
 ht.\nI'd love to offer you an exclusive first look: a product feature\, fo
 under profile\, or inclusion in an upcoming accessories roundup. I can sen
 d samples for photography\, and have high-resolution editorial images read
 y.\nPress documents including brand story\, founder bio\, editorial photog
 raphy\, and product images are Here\nI would be honoured to share this sto
 ry with your audience.\nBest\,\nIjeoma Umebeh\nFounder\nHERAE Studio | sho
 pherae.com | Instagram @shopherae
LOCATION:Virtual Event
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/herae-collection-launch-toronto/
