BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spring Blooms Hosted by The Garden Club of Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T190000
UID:blogto-234605@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/05/original_imagedaca864e-73ff-42dc-9738-161612f09e
 48.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Free Admission: Spring Blooms Returns with Stunning Florals\, 
 Live Demonstrations\, and Garden Inspiration. Thursday\, May 28th 2026\, f
 rom 2:00-7:00 p.m. at the Toronto Botanical Garden. Spring Blooms is gener
 ously sponsored by INTEGRAcare.\nSpring Blooms celebrates the very best of
  the season\, featuring breathtaking floral designs\, spectacular garden b
 looms\, and engaging live demonstrations by talented designers and horticu
 ltural experts. Visitors will enjoy an immersive experience filled with co
 lour\, fragrance\, and creativity—perfect for garden enthusiasts\, famil
 ies\, and anyone looking to be inspired by nature.\nKey Reasons for Attend
 ing:\n•	Expert Floral Design: Visitors enjoy artistic\, high-level flora
 l arrangements and horticulture displays.\n•	Member Garden Displays: The
  show highlights award-winning plants and flowers directly from club membe
 rs' gardens.\n•	Seasonal Inspiration & Education: Hourly demonstrations 
 provide inspiration for spring gardening\, featuring expert tips on plant 
 care and design.\n•	Community Connection: The event serves as a hub for 
 local garden enthusiasts to gather and celebrate the start of the season.\
 n•	Accessible Venue: It is held at the Toronto Botanical Garden\, offeri
 ng a convenient\, beautiful setting to explore.\nThe Day's Schedule:\n2:30
       Re-growing Vegetables\n3:00      A Table Arrangement\n3:30      Plan
 ning a Summer Planter (compatible plants\, containers\, number\, colour)\n
 4:00      A hand-tied bouquet\n4:30      Planting the Planter (thriller\, 
 filler\, spiller formula)\n5:00      A design using Fruit and or Vegetable
 s\n5:30      Invasive Plants to Avoid Planting in your Garden\n6:00      A
  Traditional Design water-viewing\n6:30      ReCap of Planters\, Invasives
  and Re-growing Vegetables\nGuests can also relax and recharge at the on-s
 ite Dandelion Café\, which will be open throughout the event offering foo
 d and refreshments.\nOriginally launched in 2024\, Spring Blooms was creat
 ed in response to the absence of the beloved Canada Blooms show\, which ce
 ased operations in 2020. Building on the success of the Garden Club of Tor
 onto’s long-running members-only flower and horticultural shows\, this p
 ublic event has quickly become a must-attend celebration of spring in Toro
 nto. Following overwhelmingly positive response and strong attendance in p
 revious years\, the Garden Club of Toronto is proud to bring Spring Blooms
  back in 2026—bigger\, brighter\, and more inspiring than ever.\n-------
 -\nAbout the Garden Club of Toronto (GCT)\nThe Garden Club of Toronto is a
  volunteer-based organization dedicated to promoting horticulture\, floral
  design\, and environmental stewardship through education\, community enga
 gement\, and charitable initiatives.\nSince 1947\, our Club goals have bee
 n to provide members and the public with floral design and horticultural e
 ducation\, resources\, and networking opportunities\; to provide a forum f
 or people to make new friends with people who share common interests\; to 
 promote the love of gardening\, floral design\, and civic and environmenta
 l responsibility\; and to organize and encourage participation in local an
 d international floral design shows.\nWe promote the love and knowledge of
  gardening through speakers\, symposiums\, flower shows (local and interna
 tional)\, civic garden projects\, and sponsorship of floral and landscapin
 g shows. We also fund post-secondary scholarships to students enrolled in 
 landscaping programs throughout Ontario\, as well as for the Toronto Botan
 ical Garden’s summer nature camps for youth from Toronto’s high-priori
 ty neighbourhoods.\nFor more information on the Garden Club of Toronto’s
  ongoing initiatives and future civic projects please visit our website at
  www.thegardencluboftoronto.ca.
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/spring-blooms-hosted-by-the-garden-club-
 of-toronto-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Steeped in Craft: An Evening with Chef Eva Chin x Chatime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T220000
UID:blogto-234989@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/13/original_image0d52492c-2d8b-4696-89ee-47195ac6f9
 40.jpg
DESCRIPTION:What happens when tea becomes the main ingredient instead of w
 hat’s poured into the cup?\nFor one night only\, Chatime and award-winni
 ng Yan Dining Room are coming together for Steeped in Craft — an eight-c
 ourse tasting experience that reimagines tea through contemporary Asian cu
 isine.\nHosted inside the intimate private dining room at Hong Shing\, Che
 f Eva Chin will incorporate Chatime premium teas directly into each dish 
 — from floral jasmine to smoky oolong and rich black teas — exploring 
 how tea can shape flavour\, aroma\, texture\, and storytelling throughout 
 a meal.\nLed by Chef Eva Chin\, Yan Dining Room has quickly become one of 
 Canada’s most celebrated new restaurants\, earning recognition on Air Ca
 nada’s Best New Restaurants list\, ranking #2 on Toronto Life’s Best N
 ew Restaurants of 2025\, and securing a spot on Post City’s Chef-Approve
 d 50 Best Restaurants.\nTaking place during Asian Heritage Month\, the 26-
 seat dinner marks a rare crossover between Canada’s bubble tea culture a
 nd Toronto’s fine dining scene\, blending culinary creativity\, modern A
 sian flavours\, and cultural storytelling into one immersive evening.\nEve
 nt Details\nEvent: Steeped in Craft: An Evening with Chef Eva Chin x Chati
 me\nDate: May 28\, 2026\nLocation: Yan Dining Room (private dining room in
 side Hong Shing Toronto)\nTickets: https://www.exploretock.com/hong-shing-
 toronto/experience/607743/yan-dining-room-x-chatime-canada-collaboration-d
 inner\nCost: $150 per person\nInstagram: @chatimecanada | @yandiningroom
LOCATION:Yan Dining Room
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/steeped-in-craft-an-evening-with-chef-ev
 a-chin-x-chatime-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
