BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Re.Stance Collective
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T010000
UID:blogto-234983@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/13/original_image75d81333-caf7-4028-ade6-b6e53274c5
 63.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Re.Stance is coming to Toronto this May for a weekend symposiu
 m in partnership with Textile Museum of Canada.\nFrom May 29–31\, the pr
 ogram brings together artists\, designers\, researchers\, and cultural pra
 ctitioners for a multi-day activation centered on circularity\, material i
 nnovation\, and collective futures. Positioned at the intersection of fash
 ion\, art\, and systems thinking\, the symposium explores how contemporary
  creative practices can reimagine waste\, expand material intelligence\, a
 nd contribute to more regenerative design ecosystems.\nThe opening night o
 n May 29 at The Combine sets the tone for the weekend with an immersive pu
 blic activation featuring an upcycled textile exhibition\, a curated desig
 ner showcase\, DJ sets\, and live voguing performances.\nAcross the weeken
 d\, additional programming will include panel discussions\, screenings\, w
 orkshops\, and community-led conversations that further investigate the fu
 ture of circular design and the evolving relationship between culture and 
 materiality. Together\, these activations aim to create a shared space for
  experimentation\, dialogue\, and cross-disciplinary exchange.\nDetails\nT
 ickets and updates: https://linktr.ee/re.stance\nMay 29\nAfter Hours Showc
 ase\n225 Wellington St W\n20:00 - 1:00\nthe Combine\nTextile Museum of Can
 ada\n55 centre ave\nMay 31\n13:00 - 17:00\nPanels\, Screenings\n& Workshop
 \nFor more details\, including the full program lineup\,  follow us @re.st
 ance on Instagram.\nPoster artwork by @mimisikko
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/restance-collective-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
