BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Tech Week CloseOut Afterparty
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T000000
UID:blogto-234863@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/11/original_imagecf96196d-9d39-461b-ad3e-ed2b9231a8
 99.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Partyra\, has officially partnered with Junior Jones Group to 
 present the CloseOut Party: Toronto Tech Week Socials 2026\, the closing c
 elebration for Toronto Tech Week\, taking place on Friday\, May 29\, 2026\
 , at The Pearl Events Toronto.\nBuilt as a video-first\, AI-powered event 
 discovery app\, Partyra enables users to discover nightlife\, live music\,
  social gatherings\, and cultural experiences through personalized video f
 eeds\, in-app ticketing\, and social-driven recommendations. Rather than r
 elying on static event listings\, the platform helps users experience the 
 vibe of an event before attending — creating a more intuitive and social
 ly connected way to discover what's happening in their city.\nToronto's te
 ch ecosystem deserves experiences that extend beyond conference rooms and 
 panels. This partnership with Junior Jones Group allows us to create an ex
 perience that reflects the energy\, diversity\, and culture of the city wh
 ile showcasing how Partyra is redefining event discovery and social connec
 tion.\n— Joseph Omale\, Founder\, Partyra\nAs part of the campaign\, Par
 tyra will leverage its video-first platform to drive event discovery throu
 gh immersive previews\, creator-led storytelling\, social sharing\, and re
 al-time audience engagement. The event also represents a strategic opportu
 nity for Partyra to position itself as the go-to platform for discovering 
 events across Toronto's tech\, nightlife\, and creator ecosystems.\n\nWe'r
 e excited to partner with Partyra\, the AI-powered social connection platf
 orm\, to host the official CloseOut Party for Toronto Tech Week 2026. Toro
 nto Tech Week brings together thousands of founders\, investors\, operator
 s\, and builders from around the world to celebrate innovation through com
 munity-driven events. The CloseOut Party is designed to give attendees an 
 opportunity to build meaningful connections in a relaxed atmosphere before
  transitioning into an unforgettable nightlife experience with special gue
 st DJs and interactive entertainment.\n— Junior Jones\, Junior Jones Gro
 up\n\nThe event is expected to attract a dynamic mix of tech founders\, st
 artup operators\, investors\, creatives\, and culturally connected profess
 ionals for a premium closing experience featuring guest performance by DJ 
 4KORNERS\, internationally recognized artist\, producer\, and official DJ 
 for the Toronto Raptors\, as well as feature sounds by DJ Kicks\, whose re
 nowned versatility promises a seamless musical journey\,  bringing high-en
 ergy entertainment to close out one of Canada’s biggest technology weeks
 .\nMedia Contact\nJoseph Omale\nFounder\, Partyra\njoseph.omale@partyra.co
 m\nTickets for the CloseOut Party: Toronto Tech Week Socials 2026 are now 
 available at partyra.com
LOCATION:The Pearl Events
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-tech-week-closeout-afterparty-to
 ronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Urban Garden Day Retreat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T153000
UID:blogto-234968@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/13/original_image3c093827-c770-4a88-a3fd-8de6e1c23f
 02.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Our Urban Garden Day Retreats are the perfect way to refresh w
 ithout leaving the city.\nIf you’re seeking rest\, healing\, and connect
 ion\, near to home and in a simple one-day format\, this retreat among the
  old growth trees in our English-style garden in the Beaches is for you.  
 Be Still Yoga Urban Garden Day Retreats are a special day where you’ll e
 njoy:\nThe beauty of nature: Day retreats are held in our serene\, private
  English garden and home.\nSmall-group intimacy:  We limit spaces to 10 pe
 ople at each event to create a relaxed\, personal day where we can take ca
 re of you and you can connect with other guests or spend shared time with 
 friends.\nRest & reflection time: The day unfolds in an easy\, relaxing wa
 y\, with the emphasis on connection and relaxation.  Away from the yoga ma
 ts\, there are comfy chairs\, shade\, and even a hammock.  And there’s a
 lways good food and fresh coffee on hand.\nOn-site chef: The fabulous Chef
  Mark will welcome you into the tranquil space and provide fresh\, homemad
 e and healthy drinks\, meals and snacks.\nJapanese soaker tub:  Unwind by 
 enjoying a dip in the BC Red Cedar oval tub.\nThis is a day just for you. 
  A day where we look after you.  A day when you don’t have to make decis
 ions.  A day where you can recharge\, with time for friendship\, good food
  and relaxation in this hidden gem of a garden\, here in the city.\nWhat h
 appens on the day:\n9:30am: Doors Open.  Coffee\, light breakfast and a ch
 ance to get to know the other guests in an informal\, relaxed setting.\n10
 :15 – 10:45am: Opening Circle and Satsang.  Begin the day in a supportiv
 e\, facilitated sharing space where you will have the opportunity to forge
  deep\, meaningful connections.\n11 am – 12pm: Yin Yoga Session with Kat
 hryn.  Mats\, blocks\, straps\, bolsters\, blankets\, and eye pillows are 
 all provided.\n12 – 1pm: Lunch/Free time.  Enjoy Chef Mark’s delicious
 \, healthy\, fresh food.  Share time with new or old friends in the garden
 \, on the balcony\, or under the shade of the old oak tree.\n1 – 1:45pm:
  Garden Sound Bath and Nature Experience: Sensory-guided nature experience
 . Live sound journey accompaniment to Kathryn’s sessions including gongs
 \, percussion\, chimes and crystal bowls.\n1:45 – 2:30pm: Free Time.  Bu
 ilt-in spaciousness for optional journaling\, reflection and intentional r
 est.  Healthy snacks from Mark the Chef.\n2:30 – 3:15pm Yoga Nidra Sessi
 on with Kathryn.  Calming extended meditation\, lying down in comfort and 
 listening only.\n3:30 – 4pm: Closing Circle.  An opportunity to solidify
  new friendships\, reflect on the day\, and optionally share learnings tog
 ether.\nOptional:\nPrivate Massage Therapy: Option to book in with our in-
 house registered RMT.\nPrivate Chiropractic Therapy:  Option to book in wi
 th our in-house chiropractor.
LOCATION:Be Still Yoga Garden
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/urban-garden-day-retreat-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
