BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Transient Radio: Launch Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T210000
UID:blogto-235276@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/20/original_image88bc81e9-9bd7-457b-8a91-ed3208df8f
 06.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Come celebrate the launch of Transient Radio as an emerging co
 mmunity radio station in Toronto!\nTransient Radio is an independent\, com
 munity-based online radio featuring mixes from DJs\, producers\, and music
 ians worldwide. This project has been a long time coming\, sharing weekly 
 mixes that connect Toronto's music scene to the world. So far\, the radio 
 has showcased mixes from the likes of Nabihah Iqbal\, with the intention o
 f platforming local and global talent at all levels.\nThis launch party br
 ings together an afternoon-to-evening programming rooted in community buil
 ding and open-format music exploration\, featuring:\nDiverse musical progr
 amming\, ranging from vinyl\, live hardware\, and DJ sets by Olascanola\, 
 faisalkon\, Erica (live)\, theysiii b2b international habibi\, florasystem
 \, and critter.\nA Vendor Marketplace with booths from Queers for Palestin
 e\, Disqo FM\, The Vermin Mag\, and Parallel Minds Label.\nToronto's local
  duo RAKABI will be serving South-Asian inspired sandwiches and treats thr
 oughout the event.\nOFFFFFF THE RECORD\, the collective behind Toronto's v
 ery own music card game will be hosting a chill space with carpets to gath
 er\, listen to music\, and play games while you enjoy the music.\nCome thr
 ough and be part of a day built around community\, connection\, and the pe
 ople shaping Toronto's music scene.\nGeneral admission is $19.15. Tickets 
 available at: https://ra.co/events/2428260
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/transient-radio-launch-party-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:True Chronicles... 2025\, Mayworks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T203000
UID:blogto-233876@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/20/original_image065fc483-1640-4990-94cd-0827235981
 c6.jpg
DESCRIPTION:90 minutes | Algeria\, France | French and Arabic with English
  subtitles.\nTrue Chronicles of the Blida Joinville Psychiatric Hospital i
 n the Last Century\, when Dr Frantz Fanon Was Head of the Fifth Ward betwe
 en 1953 and 1956 (2024) A film by Abdenour Zahzah\, presented with U of T 
 Community Engaged Learning Program (New College) and Centre for Caribbean 
 Studies\, Caribbean Solidarity Network\, and TPFF\nSet in French-ruled Alg
 eria in the 1950s\, before he was renowned as one of the most influential 
 thinkers and contributors to postcolonial philosophy\, Fanon was a trained
  psychiatrist. In his recently appointed position as head physician at Tru
 e Chronicles of the Blida Joinville Psychiatric Hospital in the Last Centu
 ry\, when Dr Frantz Fanon Was Head of the Fifth Ward between 1953 and 1956
  (2024) the Blida-Joinville Hospital\, a young Fanon witnesses the racist 
 and Islamaphobic cruelty the hospital’s patients endured. Filmed in the 
 same hospital where Fanon once worked\, the film explores this short but i
 mpactful chapter of his life using archival records and Fanon’s hospital
  diaries.\nRegister at mayworks.ca\nThis venue has wheelchair accessible b
 athrooms and a wheelchair accessible venue
LOCATION:Alliance Francaise Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/true-chronicles-2025-mayworks-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:UCL Final Watch Party: PSG vs Arsenal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T143000
UID:blogto-235079@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/15/original_imagec990afc7-afdd-48c1-8a76-cc9b07c3b3
 c8.jpg
DESCRIPTION:FREE TO ATTEND! ⚽\nOn Saturday\, May 30 at 11:30 AM\, Toront
 o26 is bringing PSG vs Arsenal to Bloor Street for what we’re calling To
 ronto’s biggest UCL Final watch party\, hosted across two side-by-side v
 enues: Crafty Coyote and Mezcalero. 🏟️🔥\nOne match. Two venues. On
 e massive afternoon for football fans in the city.\nWhether you’re backi
 ng PSG\, riding with Arsenal\, or just showing up for the biggest club mat
 ch of the season\, this is where you want to be. 🔴⚪️🔵\nWe’ll b
 e taking over:\nCrafty Coyote\n511 Bloor St W\nMezcalero\n509 Bloor St W\n
 Expect big match energy\, packed rooms\, giveaways\, good people\, and the
  kind of atmosphere Toronto keeps proving it can deliver. ⚽🍻\nWe’ll
  have tons of giveaways\, including jerseys and more\, plus special prizes
  from our friends at AFC Toronto\, Inter Toronto FC\, and Hollow Valley Sp
 irits.\nAnd this one means a little more.\nBy attending\, you’ll also be
  supporting Extra Time for Toronto\, a charitable partnership between Toro
 nto26 and Second Harvest helping turn football community energy into real 
 local impact.\nTwo side-by-side venues. One final. Toronto football showin
 g up again.\nDoors open early\, so get there ahead of kickoff\, grab your 
 spot\, and let the atmosphere build.\nSaturday afternoons don’t get much
  bigger than this. 🌟\nWho is Toronto26?\nWe run Toronto’s top soccer 
 watch parties\, building hype for 2026 while helping grow the city’s soc
 cer culture. Through high-energy events and community collaborations\, we 
 bring fans\, local businesses\, and neighbourhoods together around the gam
 e.\nToronto26 is also part of the Matchday Social network\, a growing move
 ment that connects supporters beyond the stadium by turning local pubs and
  community spaces into matchday hubs where football culture can thrive.\nB
 ecause the game isn’t only played on the pitch. It lives wherever fans g
 ather.\nToronto is a soccer city.\nwww.toronto26.com | info@toronto26.com 
 | info@matchdaysocial.com | #TorontoIsASoccerCity\n* Independent watch par
 ty. Not affiliated with or endorsed by UEFA\, the Champions League\, Arsen
 al or PSG.
LOCATION:Crafty Coyote
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/ucl-final-watch-party-psg-vs-arsenal-tor
 onto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
