BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Connect & Release: Blue Moon Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T180000
UID:blogto-235313@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/20/original_imageed3bb261-2956-433c-a082-4786c99865
 ae.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A monthly circle to slow down\, reconnect\, and honour your in
 ner world in a safe\, supportive space.\nEach circle offers a safe\, nurtu
 ring container to slow down\, turn inward\, and listen to your intuition. 
 Through guided practices\, reflection\, and shared presence\, we create sp
 ace to release what no longer serves and reconnect with our deepest inner 
 wisdom.\n✨ What to Expect\nThese circles are an invitation to:\nConnect 
 with your intuition and emotional landscape\nHonour nature’s cycles and 
 the wisdom of the full moon\nGently release stress\, old patterns\, and em
 otional weight\nReconnect with your deep inner self and inner voice\nExper
 ience belonging and community in a safe\, compassionate space\nRelax\, gro
 und\, and re-centre amidst everyday life\nThis is a time to express yourse
 lf authentically\, be witnessed\, and feel supported — exactly as you ar
 e. No prior experience is necessary.\n🌕 Who This Is For\nThose feeling 
 called to deepen their intuition\nAnyone seeking emotional release\, groun
 ding\, and clarity\nIntuitive\, sensitive\, or spiritually curious individ
 uals\nThose longing for authentic connection and community\n✨ Come as yo
 u are. Leave feeling lighter\, clearer\, and more connected.\nSpaces are l
 imited to preserve an intimate and supportive container.\n🌕 2026 Key Da
 tes\n✨ Blue Moon: Sunday\, May 31 | 4:00 – 6:00 PM\n✨ Strawberry Moo
 n: Sunday\, June 28 | 4:00 – 6:00 PM\n✨ Buck Moon: Thursday\, July 30 
 | 7:00 – 9:00 PM\n✨ Sturgeon Moon: Sunday\, August 30 | 4:00 – 6:00 
 PM\n✨ Harvest Moon: Sunday\, September 27 | 4:00 – 6:00 PM\n✨ Hunter
 's Moon: Sunday\, October 25 | 4:00 – 6:00 PM\n✨ Beaver Moon: Sunday\,
  November 22 | 4:00 – 6:00 PM\n✨ Cold Moon: Sunday\, December 20 | 4:0
 0 – 6:00 PM\n🧘 What to Bring\nA journal and pen for reflection and in
 tegration\nComfortable clothing that allows you to relax and move with eas
 e\n🌿 About Esné\nMy name is Esné\, and I am a Certified Clinical Hypn
 osis Specialist & Somatic Practitioner. My work serves those who have hit 
 a standstill on their healing path and find themselves repeating patterns 
 despite their best efforts to move beyond them.\nI am not interested in cl
 inical diagnoses or labels\; I want to know who you are as a person. Based
  on your unique imprint\, I use a blend of evidence-based tools and deep i
 ntuitive insight to guide you toward a deeper understanding of self.\nThis
  is a space where your humanity is honoured and your personal power reclai
 med.\nhttps://naturalesne.com\nInstagram @natural.esne\n“Being able to f
 eel safe with other people is probably the single most important aspect of
  mental health\; safe connections are fundamental to meaningful and satisf
 ying lives.”\n― Bessel A. van der Kolk\, The Body Keeps the Score: Bra
 in\, Mind\, and Body in the Healing of Trauma\n🏡 About the Inner Arts C
 ollective\nInner Arts Collective (IAC) is a community of professionals off
 ering services for the body\, mind\, and soul\, supporting individuals\, f
 amilies\, teams\, and communities.\nIAC is a safe and compassionate oasis 
 for self-care and personal development. Together\, the collective creates 
 a safe healing space\, bringing health\, positive energy\, and personal de
 velopment opportunities to each other\, our communities\, and the planet.\
 nThe Inner Arts Collective is deeply grateful for the support of its local
  and global community\, families\, and clients — supporting one another 
 through both the good times and the challenges.\nwww.innerartscollective.c
 om
LOCATION:Inner Arts Collective
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/connect-release-blue-moon-circle-toronto
 /
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
