  and beyond. From fried beignets and bubble waffles to Jamaican patties\, 
 tacos\, bagels\, pizza and more\, the festival invites attendees to experi
 ence a food festival with delicious gluten-free food and zero gluten-relat
 ed worry\, showcasing bold\, globally inspired flavours and the very best 
 of today’s GF scene.\nThis year’s not-to-miss food moments include Riz
  Gluten Free’s pop-up serving bánh mì\, ramen and Vietnamese street fo
 od\, Montreal favourites like soft pretzels from Delicious Without Gluten 
 and Parisian-style pastries from L’Artisan Délices Sans Gluten\, and Tr
 u Delite’s signature bubble waffles. Guests can also look forward to a c
 racker charcuterie experience and a wide range of sweet and savoury festiv
 al favourites throughout the day.\nThe event has become a must-attend for 
 Toronto’s growing gluten-free community\, drawing hundreds eager to disc
 over new products\, meet makers and experience a world of flavours.\nTimed
 -entry tickets are $16 online\, with limited availability at the door\, an
 d free entry for kids 15 and under. A community food drive\, run by Celiac
  Canada\, will support The Beeton Cupboard and Fort York Food Bank.
