BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Graham Greene Tribute Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T230000
UID:blogto-234762@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/07/original_imagef43035bd-fc88-4f43-a4f7-36a2c00a81
 c2.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Toronto\, this is your chance to celebrate a true icon of Indi
 genous cinema 🎥✨\nJoin us for an unforgettable evening celebrating th
 e incredible career and legacy of Graham Greene at the Graham Greene Tribu
 te Night on June 1\, 2026\, at the Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema in Toronto. 
 Doors open at 6:30 PM for an evening of film\, reflection\, and community 
 celebration.\nFrom iconic films like Thunderheart\, Dances with Wolves\, a
 nd The Green Mile\, Graham Greene has inspired generations through powerfu
 l storytelling and unforgettable performances — and now the community is
  coming together to honour his impact on film and Indigenous representatio
 n.\nThe night will feature a special screening of Thunderheart\, reflectio
 ns from guest speakers\, community celebration\, and a chance to experienc
 e an evening filled with culture\, storytelling\, nostalgia\, and connecti
 on.\nWhether you’re a longtime film lover\, supporter of Indigenous arts
 \, or simply looking for a meaningful and memorable night out in Toronto\,
  this is an event you won’t want to miss.\nEven better? All proceeds fro
 m the event will be donated to imagineNATIVE Film + Media Arts Festival\, 
 supporting the next generation of Indigenous filmmakers and storytellers.\
 nTickets are on sale now through Eventbrite — secure your spot before th
 ey’re gone!\nFilm lovers\, community supporters\, and culture enthusiast
 s — this is a night worth experiencing.🍿
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/graham-greene-tribute-night-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lost Wax Ring Casting Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T210000
UID:blogto-232272@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/17/original_image12e6f9d8-6ef1-4d27-8617-02a79b8ded
 a8.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by the remarkable discoveries at the Roman Vindolanda
  Fort\, this hands-on workshop explores the ancient art of lost wax ring c
 asting (known to ancient Romans cire perdue) with the Fort York Metal Co.\
 nAt Vindolanda\, archaeologists uncovered everything from leather shoes to
  personal letters\, revealing the everyday lives of Roman soldiers and civ
 ilians stationed at the edge of the empire. Among these finds were beautif
 ully crafted personal adornments\, such as rings that symbolized identity\
 , status\, devotion\, and love.\nIn this immersive workshop\, you’ll lea
 rn the same centuries-old lost wax process Roman artisans used to create d
 etailed metal jewelry. Carve and shape your own wax ring design\, drawing 
 inspiration from Roman motifs\, military insignia\, or symbols of personal
  meaning. Your design will then be taken away and cast in silver metal\, t
 ransforming your wax model into a lasting\, wearable artifact.\nWhether yo
 u’re fascinated by ancient craftsmanship\, intrigued by life on Rome’s
  northern frontier\, or simply eager to create something uniquely your own
 \, this workshop connects modern makers to the artistry and ingenuity of t
 he ancient world.\nRing carving workshop\, metal casting\, museum access d
 uring the event time\, and light refreshments included.\nPLEASE NOTE: Ring
 s will not be cast on site. After the rings are carved\, they will be take
 n away to be cast by Fort York Metal Co. Participants will be notified as 
 to when they can return to the BSM to pick up their finished rings\, and m
 ust do two within two weeks of being notified.
LOCATION:Bata Shoe Museum
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/lost-wax-ring-casting-workshop-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
