BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flames Launches High-Performance Summer Volleyball Training Progra
 m
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T140000
UID:blogto-235015@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/14/original_imagec3f84617-0785-4f4f-9176-0a92139b1a
 77.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Date & Time:\nEvening Sessions: Tuesdays & Thursdays starting 
 June 2\, 2026\nDaytime Training: Monday–Thursday starting June 8\, 2026 
 (excluding first week of August)\nLocations: Multiple locations in Burling
 ton\, Ontario\, including: Robert Bateman Community Centre\, Alton Communi
 ty Centre\, and  Tansley Wood Community Centre\nRegistration: https://www.
 flamesvolleyball.com/summer-training\nPricing: Starting at $50 per session
 \; $80 for full-day training blocks\nEvent Description\nFlames Volleyball 
 is launching its Summer Volleyball Training Program\, a high-performance t
 raining environment led by current U SPORTS athletes\, OUA competitors\, a
 nd elite-level guest coaches. Sessions are delivered in small groups\, wit
 h a maximum of 15 athletes and an approximate 5:1 athlete-to-coach ratio\,
  ensuring focused instruction and meaningful reps. Training emphasizes gam
 e-speed drills\, high-repetition skill development\, and tactical gameplay
 \, with a strong focus on decision-making under pressure. Athletes will al
 so benefit from integrated speed\, agility\, and movement work\, along wit
 h competitive open gym and live-play sessions. Throughout the summer\, gue
 st coaching appearances add additional layers of insight and elite-level e
 xperience.\nThe summer-long coaching lineup includes:\nWill Brewer - Outsi
 de Hitter for the Windsor Lancers\; Team Ontario Elite\; OVA Champion\, an
 d two-time OUA Silver Medalist\nMatt Powell - Matthew Powell was named the
  2026 Canadian Collegiate Athletic Association Men’s Volleyball Coach of
  the Year after leading the Seneca Sting.  Known for his focus on leadersh
 ip\, accountability\, and holistic student-athlete development\, Powell ha
 s built a culture of excellence both on and off the court. His impact has 
 quickly positioned Seneca as one of the top rising programs in Canadian co
 llegiate volleyball.\nKai Taylor- Outside Hitter for Toronto Metropolitan 
 University\; U-16 indoor national championship\, as well as a bronze medal
  at nationals for beach volleyball.\nMarko Milenkovic - Team Ontario coach
  and former TMU athlete\; Marko Milenkovic is a Team Ontario Coach and for
 mer TMU/Ryerson athlete. He is a 3-time U Sports Academic All-Star Canadia
 n\, and 3-time OUA Academic Achievement Award. Before Ryerson he spent fiv
 e years as a key member of the Toronto West VBC (2009-2014). He served fou
 r years as captain of the Toronto West VBC and was awarded Jr. Boys MVP (2
 012-13) and Sr. Boys MVP (2013-14) while playing for Richview Collegiate I
 nstitute.\nFeatured guest coaching appearances throughout the summer also 
 include: Matt Powell\, CCAA Coach of the Year\, who will be leading Tuesda
 y evening sessions in June.\nAdditional university and high-performance gu
 est coaches to be announced in the coming weeks…
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/flames-launches-high-performance-summer-
 volleyball-training-program-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Forest Raiser!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T210000
UID:blogto-234167@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/25/original_imagef2ef13cc-d4e2-40d3-919c-f1e07db293
 fe.jpg
DESCRIPTION:​Forest-Raiser. An evening to raise funds and awareness for 
 forest conservation and reforestation initiatives.\n​Forests are among o
 ur most vital ecosystems — providing habitat\, regulating climate\, and 
 sustaining life across the planet. This Toronto Climate Week\, we invite y
 ou to celebrate and support the organizations working to protect them.\n
 ​Mix and mingle over nature-inspired mocktails\, soulful jazz\, and plan
 t-forward delicacies. Immerse yourself in eco-arts and connect with like-m
 inded individuals.\n​Most important (!) Hear from three purpose-driven o
 rganizations and support their work through our silent auction.\n​This y
 ear’s beneficiaries are:\n​• FSC (Forest Stewardship Council) — Th
 e Forest Stewardship Council (FSC) sets the gold standard for responsible 
 forest management.\n​• Flash Forest — Modernizing forestry through d
 ata-driven automation.\n​• LEAF (Local Enhancement & Appreciation of F
 orests) — Engaging GTA communities in urban forest planting\, stewardshi
 p and education.\n​Forest-Raiser Tuesday\, June 2nd\, 2026 | 6:00 – 9:
 00 PM Centre for Social Innovation\, Toronto\n​We look forward to coming
  together for an evening that invests in our forests\, and the future they
  make possible for all species.\n​A huge thank you to our volunteers and
  sponsors making the event possible. Let’s toast one to the trees!
LOCATION:Centre for Social Innovation
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/forest-raiser-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
