BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beyond Words: Addressing Anti-Black Racism and Discriminatory Lang
 uage in Schools
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T203000
UID:blogto-234979@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/13/original_imagecd7bb556-8310-40c3-ac60-835130f7a1
 eb.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Language plays a powerful role in shaping what is tolerated\, 
 ignored\, challenged\, or normalized in schools. Harmful language doesn’
 t exist in isolation—it impacts how students experience safety\, belongi
 ng\, and stability.\nJoin us for an evening of meaningful conversation abo
 ut language\, belonging\, anti-Black racism\, and school culture in our fo
 urth annual live podcast event.\nIn partnership with Harmony Movement\, Un
 iversity of Toronto Schools\, and Unsinkable\, our discussion will feature
  4 panelists who will explore the role of language in both reinforcing har
 m and creating the conditions for more respectful\, inclusive\, and courag
 eous school communities.\nHosted by Asante Haughton and Kritika Sharda\, t
 he discussion will explore what responsibility different community members
  hold and what it takes to build environments rooted in dignity\, accounta
 bility\, repair\, and inclusion.\nRemaining true to The 44 North principle
  of grounding discussion in action\, panelists will not only share what ne
 eds to change\, but who has the power to create that change\, and what cou
 rage and responsibility look like in practice. Rather than asking young pe
 ople to share painful experiences for the benefit of others\, the event is
  designed to honour youth insight\, wisdom\, agency\, and vision.\nTickets
  available on Eventbrite: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/live-podcast-event-b
 eyond-words-tickets-1987686053493
LOCATION:University of Toronto Schools
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/beyond-words-addressing-anti-black-racis
 m-and-discriminatory-language-in-schools-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
