BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Killer B Cinema Presents: Pulgasari!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T223000
UID:blogto-235086@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/15/original_imaged80c7975-1e8a-4d48-9d59-cf8af5a638
 27.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us on June 5th for the North Korean Kaiju movie Pulgasari
 ! You heard that right! North Korea! We’ve got a tale to tell you about 
 its making as well!\nAdvanced tickets are $5 or $8 at the door (Space is l
 imited\, and tickets sell out fast)!\nhttps://www.eventbrite.ca/e/killer-b
 -cinema-presents-pulgasari-tickets-1988676003460?aff=oddtdtcreator\nDoors 
 open at 7:30 pm\, and the movie begins at 8:00.\n*NO outside food or drink
 s\; please buy food and drinks from the venue.\n*All films have closed cap
 tioning.\nMovie info:\nPulgasari  is a 1986 monster film directed and pr
 oduced by Shin Sang-ok during his North Korean abduction. A co-production 
 between North Korea\, Japan\, and China\, it is supposedly a remake of Bul
 gasari\, a 1962 South Korean film that also depicts Bulgasari/Pulgasari\, 
 a creature from Korean folklore. The ensemble cast includes Chang Sŏnhŭi
 \, Ham Kisŏp\, Ri Chongguk\, Ri Ingwŏn\, and Yu Kyŏngae\, with Kenpachi
 ro Satsuma in the title role. Set during the Goryeo dynasty\, Pulgasari fo
 llows a blacksmith's daughter who brings to life a metal-eating monster he
 r late father created to defeat the monarchy. {Wikipedia}\nInfo about See-
 Scape:\nOur movies will be shown on the second floor! There are two bars a
 vailable in See-Scape. The bar is open on the second floor during our even
 t and is cash only. Debit/Credit purchases are available on the main floor
 .\nSee-Scape also has an amazing menu. To learn more about See-Scape\, ple
 ase click here! https://www.seescapeto.com/\nSee-Scape is located at 347 K
 eele Street (the closest intersection is Keele/Dundas) and is easily acces
 sible via TTC. (from Keele Station or Dundas West Station)\nParking: There
  is a Green P parking lot beside See-Scape and a few other paid parking lo
 ts nearby.\nEach month\, join Lizzie Violet & Zoltan Du Lac for killer B-m
 oves from the 1930s to the present!\nPlease like our Facebook page and Ins
 tagram @killerbcinema so you don’t miss an invite.\nThank you to See-Sca
 pe and their staff! They make our monthly event extra unforgettable!\nWe h
 ope to see you at See-Scape.
LOCATION:See-Scape
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/killer-b-cinema-presents-pulgasari-toron
 to/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Louise The Last Dance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T210000
UID:blogto-234785@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/07/original_imagebada6d7e-e2b2-49e7-bcf7-f4158de52d
 7a.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Louise: The Last Dance | June 5 & 19 @ Society Clubhouse\nToro
 nto\, meet Louise Weber: the working-class woman who invented the cancan\,
  became the most famous entertainer in Europe\, and died selling peanuts o
 n the street outside the same club that made her a star. You've never hear
 d of her. That's kind of the whole point.\nLouise: The Last Dance is a new
  solo theatre show by Saint Stella\, the Toronto performer behind three co
 nsecutive sold-out Fringe hits — and it's heading to the Edinburgh Festi
 val Fringe this August. But first: two nights only at Society Clubhouse.\n
 June 5 is the world premiere preview\, with a talkback after the show. Bri
 ng your feedback voice!\nJune 19 is a full party: the show\, then a burles
 que showcase with Arra Kiss\, Cleo Tantra\, Evelyn Crane\, Maximum Capacit
 y\, and Sugar Holiday\, then a dance party with DJs Melelectric and Butt M
 itzfah. Art party on!\nDoors at 7pm . Show at 7:30pm\nBoth nights are pay-
 what-you-can cash at the door.\nOr donate any amount at https://fnd.us/52h
 HN3?ref=sh_6EoXI2 to get on the list and help send Louise to Edinburgh.
LOCATION:Society Clubhouse
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/louise-the-last-dance-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
