BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Zoo - Haudenosaunee Star Teachings
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T203000
UID:blogto-235205@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/19/original_imagefe253d8b-7782-42a7-8ed4-cc250a2c33
 d0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Indigenous Astronomy: Filling your Spirit with Stardust and As
 tronomical Knowledge\nSamantha Doxtator\, Haudenosaunee-Oneida\, Wolf Clan
 \, is a Personal Development Consultant whose work is rooted in traditiona
 l values. She carries forward a legacy on Indigenous astronomical knowledg
 e\, continuing work gifted to her by her late sister\, Sasha Doxtator who 
 passed away in 2021. Her presentations invite audiences to reflect\, recon
 nect\, and reimagine their relationship with the universe.\nIndigenous Ast
 ronomy: Filling your Spirit with Stardust and Astronomical Knowledge\nSama
 ntha Doxtator\, Haudenosaunee-Oneida\, Wolf Clan\, is a Personal Developme
 nt Consultant whose work is rooted in traditional values. She carries forw
 ard a legacy on Indigenous astronomical knowledge\, continuing work gifted
  to her by her late sister\, Sasha Doxtator who passed away in 2021. Her p
 resentations invite audiences to reflect\, reconnect\, and reimagine their
  relationship with the universe.
LOCATION:Toronto Zoo
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-zoo-haudenosaunee-star-teachings
 -toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ultras
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T210800
UID:blogto-235047@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/14/original_image74b9ff70-0ce8-4770-9ab6-144f34e6ce
 7c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Feast your senses on this visceral and electrifying mosaic of 
 soccer’s uber fans\, famed for staging monumental collective displays th
 at transform global stadiums into churning cauldrons of sound and colour. 
 Known as “ultras\,” these hardcore supporters often contribute as much
  to the match-day atmosphere as the on-pitch action. They’ve also been k
 nown to clash with authority—a byproduct of the rebellious energy and co
 ntagious fervour that powers this worldwide subculture. Filmmaker Ragnhild
  Ekner extends an insider’s invitation to meet vibrant fan communities i
 n Argentina\, Egypt\, England\, Indonesia\, Italy\, Morocco\, Poland and S
 weden. Her approach is thrillingly cinematic and deeply immersive\, exalti
 ng in the spirit of defiant fellowship that is pushing back against the st
 eady commodification of the beautiful game. Before FIFA brings its flagshi
 p product to Toronto next summer\, Ultras is your ticket to an authentical
 ly awe-inspiring terrace experience. Julian Carrington\, Hot Docs 2025\nIn
  Swedish\, English\, Arabic\, Indonesian\, Italian\, Polish and Spanish\, 
 with English subtitles.\nContent Warning: Contains flashing lights.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/ultras-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
