ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/08/original_imageb0770430-7ce9-4dfc-9d14-518cb7831e
 2d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:One of Toronto’s largest tours of private gardens. Garden-go
 ers will have the opportunity to visit 12 residential gardens\, in the uni
 que Toronto enclave of the Beach or as some call it\, the Beaches. We make
  it easy to get around with complimentary shuttle buses you can “hop on 
 and hop off” at garden stops along the route. The garden tour area is al
 so very walkable (and beautiful).\nKnowledgeable Toronto Master Gardeners 
 are stationed in each garden to answer your plant and garden design questi
 ons. While you’re touring\, look forward to other pop-up interactions in
 cluding live music\, local ravine experts and a street fair in the charmin
 g Kingston Road Village. Thanks to our partnership with The Beach BIA you
 ’ll have access to digital walking routes that connect to local business
 es and the surrounding natural/public spaces.\nThis outdoor event can be e
 njoyed solo or with family and friends\, strolling along the tree-lined st
 reets\, while skipping in and out of gardens. When you purchase your ticke
 t you'll receive a Wildflower seed paper wristband (which you can plant la
 ter) that will give you access to the gardens\, and a self-guided map so y
 ou can discover tour at your own pace.\nCome early or linger after the tou
 r to shop or dine at one of the local restaurants or boutiques in the area
 . There is no other neighbourhood quite like The Beach.\nTickets can be pu
 rchased online.\nOne-Day Pass\, Public $45\, TBG Member $40\nTwo-Day Pass\
 , Public $70\, TBG Member $65\nStudent/Child Pass\, $25\nAll proceeds supp
 ort the Toronto Botanical Garden
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/through-the-garden-gate-the-beach-toront
 o/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
