 bb.jpg
DESCRIPTION:While June is quieter than the spring migration rush in April 
 and May\, there’s still lots happening in Toronto’s High Park! Summer 
 residents have settled into their groove and they’re busy raising young 
 and some are eating as much as they can because fall migration is right ar
 ound the corner.\nThis is a beginner-friendly hike. The Nature Centre will
  have binoculars to borrow for the event.\nPrice: Pay What You Can (FREE\,
  $5\, $8\, $10)\nAges: 16+ years
LOCATION:High Park Forest School
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/june-early-summer-birding-walk-in-toront
 os-high-park-toronto/
