 80.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join acclaimed author Lucy Sante for a special talk exploring 
 Larry Fink’s role as a social photographer\, examining both his social e
 ngagement and his commitment to documenting society.\nPeople and their int
 eractions were central to Fink's work. Over a career spanning more than si
 xty years\, he photographed debutante balls\, Oscar parties\, demonstratio
 ns\, boxing matches\, and his neighbours in rural Pennsylvania—all with 
 bold framing and masterly chiaroscuro\, and with urgency\, immediacy\, and
  deep human feeling.\nPresented in conjunction with the exhibition "Larry 
 Fink: Social Graces & Runway" on view at The Image Centre.\nLecture Room: 
 IMA-307\nEnter via: The Image Centre\n33 Gould Street\, Toronto\nPlease ha
 ve your Eventbrite registration and valid ID ready upon arrival. The name 
 on your ID must match the name on your ticket or registration. All bags ma
 y be subject to inspection by gallery security upon entry.\nWith support f
 rom Muus Collection.\nImage: Larry Fink\, Skating Rink\, PA\, 1980 (printe
 d later) gelatin silver print © Larry Fink/MUUS Collection. The Image Cen
 tre\, Gift of Gordon Fenwick\, 2021
