DESCRIPTION:Citadel LIVE presents\nAh W.I. Ting\nCo-presented with KasheDa
 nce\nChoreographed by Kevin A. Ormsby and Jillia Cato\n \nJune 18-20\, 20
 26 @ 8pm\nAt The Citadel: Ross Centre for Dance\nAh W.I. Ting blends Carib
 bean jazz with choreography inspired by Tobago’s Tambrin music. Caribbea
 n jazz\, rooted in Afro-Caribbean folk traditions and dance\, has had a si
 gnificant yet often overlooked impact on the broader jazz scene\, particul
 arly in the U.S. Unlike American jazz\, Ah W.I. Ting focuses on Caribbean 
 dance\, incorporating contemporary elements while highlighting the extempo
  rhythm and time signatures of calypso and soca music.
LOCATION:The Citadel: Ross Centre for Dance
