BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ANCHORBALL: A Curious Art Journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T170000
UID:blogto-235048@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/14/original_image103bb49d-17f5-4db5-b965-e66e8e84d6
 6e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Canadian premiere of ANCHORBALL: A Curious Art Journey is 
 coming to Royal Botanical Gardens this summer!\nExplore the vibrant sculpt
 ural universe of artist and contemporary sculptor Ken Kelleher\, internati
 onally known as Anchorball. This massive outdoor exhibition transforms the
  garden into a vivid sculptural landscape where bold characters\, imaginat
 ive narratives\, and contemporary form merge with nature and blooms to cre
 ate a world that feels full of wonder\, yet deeply recognizable.\nFeaturin
 g 18 monumental sculptures ranging up to 12 feet tall\, the exhibition int
 roduces visitors to an evolving fictional universe populated by playful an
 d mythical characters. Visitors can also discover a hidden digital world u
 sing augmented reality\, extending the experience beyond the visible lands
 cape and inviting moments of surprise\, play\, and exploration throughout 
 the garden\nCome experience a joyful fusion of nature and art designed for
  curiosity\, fun\, exploration\, and imagination.\nBook your tickets now a
 t rbg.ca/anchorball.\nDates: June 20 - September 20\, 2026\nTimes: 10 a.m.
  to 5 p.m. (final admission: 4 p.m.)\nAges: All Ages\nLocation: Hendrie Pa
 rk\, Royal Botanical Gardens\, 680 Plains Rd W\, Burlington\, ON L7T 4H4\n
 Ticket Prices:  General Tickets: Non-Members $19.50 - $24.50 (Prices subje
 ct to HST and online service fee). Members: FREE access\nWebsite: rbg.ca\n
 Connect & Share on our Social Channels:\nInstagram:@rbgcanada\nFacebook: R
 oyal Botanical Gardens\nTikTok: @rbgcanada\nTags: RBGAnchorball
LOCATION:Royal Botanical Gardens
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/anchorball-a-curious-art-journey-toronto
 /
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anga's Farm: Open Terrarium Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T170000
UID:blogto-233738@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/16/original_image42443230-7052-4782-9a0a-475bbdb36e
 c0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Workshop: Open Terrarium Creation | Build Your Own Mini Jungle
 \nCreate your own miniature world of green! In this hands-on workshop\, yo
 u’ll design and build a beautiful open terrarium set in a modern glass v
 essel with a natural wooden base.\nYou’ll be guided step-by-step through
  the entire process\, from layering different soils and drainage materials
  to selecting and arranging your plants. Using a mix of decorative rocks\,
  moss\, and natural accents\, you’ll create a unique piece that fits you
 r style.\nParticipants will:\nCreate their own open terrarium using a sele
 ction of tropical plants\nLearn how to properly layer soil\, drainage\, an
 d decorative elements\nExplore different design styles using rocks\, moss\
 , and natural textures\nGain simple\, practical care tips to keep their te
 rrarium healthy and thriving\nEvery terrarium is unique\, and you’ll hav
 e the freedom to make it your own\, whether you prefer something lush and 
 full or clean and minimal. By the end of the session\, you’ll take home 
 a beautiful\, low-maintenance indoor garden—perfect for brightening your
  space or gifting to someone special. This workshop is beginner-friendly a
 nd a fun\, creative way to spend time with plants.\nVisit our website for 
 more details & to sign up! www.angasfarm.ca
LOCATION:Anga's Farm & Nursery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/angas-farm-open-terrarium-workshop-toron
 to/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annual U2 Day in Toronto - FREE
