ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/18/original_image3fd9a17a-513a-4a11-857c-1a9aaf092b
 56.jpg
DESCRIPTION:It's ALL U2 - all day.\nFREE. OVER 100 door prizes - Fantastic
  door prizes every hour.\nALL U2 on 11 TVs with BIG sound\, BIG lights. Bi
 g\, immersive entertainment.\n**** Legendary Canadian broadcaster ALAN CRO
 SS talks U2 and answers your U2 questions at 7pm\nOVER 100 door prizes - H
 OURLY door prizes\, including retro Victrola record players (but with blue
 tooth too) complete with U2 coloured vinyl records to go with each on. And
  custom U2 bluetooth speakers - pre-loaded with U2's biggest hits. Alan Cr
 oss books too.\nU2 TRIBUTE DAY - TORONTO TAKES ON THE EDGE!\nGet ready\, T
 oronto! The spirit of Ireland is coming to our city with a day dedicated t
 o the legendary rock band U2!\nMark your calendars for U2 Tribute Day in T
 oronto - Saturday\, June 20th- a Corso Italia celebration where the street
  will echo with the anthems of freedom\, love\, and rock 'n' roll. Toronto
  is set to transform into a one-day U2 utopia!\nThis isn't just a tribute\
 , it's a day where Toronto unites under the banner of U2's music\, a testa
 ment to their lasting impact and our city's love for unforgettable music e
 xperiences.\nDon't miss out on this epic tribute to one of the greatest ba
 nds of all time. Whether you're a lifelong fan or just love good music\, U
 2 Tribute Day in Toronto promises to be a day where we all stand together\
 , singing out loud for the pure joy of it.\nSave the date\, wear your best
  U2 gear\, and let's make some unforgettable memories together in Toronto!
  #U2TorontoTribute #OneLoveUnderTheEdge\n*** note - this is a "tribute" ev
 ent with licensed\, pre-recorded music and video. No live performances are
  scheduled and members of U2 are not appearing. But of course Bono and the
  boys are welcome to drop by!
LOCATION:The Cat's Cradle
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/annual-u2-day-in-toronto-free-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
