BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Peterborough Musicfest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T220000
UID:blogto-230217@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/02/02/original_image45ca9347-62fd-40cf-8e84-3bc91cf100
 86.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Peterborough Musicfest is one of Ontario’s longest-running f
 ree outdoor concert series — and an easy summer escape just about 1.5 ho
 urs from Toronto. Set at Del Crary Park on the shores of Little Lake\, the
  series brings live music to the waterfront every Wednesday and Saturday n
 ight from the end of June to mid August.\nThe lineup features a mix of Can
 adian and international artists across rock\, pop\, country\, indie\, folk
 \, and roots\, with the Future Sound Series presented by Cogeco local act 
 at 6:30 pm and the headliner on stage at 8:00 pm. Past seasons have includ
 ed Down With Webster\, Gob\, Metric\, Dallas Green\, Sloan\, Steven Page a
 nd more.\nConcerts are free\, outdoors\, and family-friendly\, with plenty
  of space for lawn chairs and blankets. On-site food vendors and nearby pa
 tios make it easy to turn the night into a full evening out\, while the su
 rrounding Kawarthas offer beaches\, trails\, cycling routes\, and cottage-
 country vibes for anyone making a weekend of it.\nIf you’re looking for 
 live music under the stars without the ticket price Peterborough Musicfest
  is a summer staple worth the drive.
LOCATION:Del Crary Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/peterborough-musicfest-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
