 5e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Summer Music returns for its 2026 Festival\, under the
  fresh direction of Artistic Director William Fedkenheuer! The year will b
 ring artists listening deeply\, audiences leaning in\, and a city gatherin
 g around something meaningful.\nThis season brings together extraordinary 
 voices\, featuring the renowned Les Arts Florissants on Opening Night with
  a double-bill of Charpentier. For the chamber music lovers\, you can hear
  the Miró\, Poiesis\, and Balourdet Quartets\, as well as members of the 
 Dover\, Calidore\, Viano\, New Orford\, and Brentano String Quartets. Bel 
 canto superstars Erin Morley and Lawrence Brownlee present their celebrate
 d Golden Age program — one of the top 25 albums of 2025 by the New York 
 Times.\nGold Laureate of the 2025 Honens International Piano Competition 
 Élisabeth Pion makes her Toronto debut alongside harpist Emmanuel Ceysson
  with the TSM Festival Orchestra\, under the baton of Ryan Haskins. Other 
 performances include mezzo-soprano Sasha Cooke\, pianist Inon Barnatan\, v
 iolinist Timothy Chooi in recital with pianist Jon Kimura Parker\, with a 
 program dedicated to Jascha Heifetz\, Kleztory\, members of the Chamber Mu
 sic Society of Lincoln Center\, and more! Come get your classical music fi
 x for summer\, with 50+ events between July 9 - August 1!
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-summer-music-festival-toronto-3/
