ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/19/original_image1921d3ea-f826-4327-a3b4-977906312d
 7a.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Music has always carried us somewhere — across landscapes\, 
 through memory\, into the heart. Clara Schumann’s Three Romances open th
 e evening with intimacy and poetic warmth. Kevin Lau’s String Quartet No
 . 5\, “The Train to Improbable Places”\, invites us on a vivid contemp
 orary journey fueled by imagination. Mendelssohn’s radiant Op. 44 Quarte
 t sings with lyrical brilliance\, and Dvořák’s beloved Piano Quintet b
 rings the evening home with folk-inspired vitality and sweeping Romantic j
 oy. An evening of movement\, storytelling\, and music that transports.
LOCATION:Walter Hall
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-summer-music-improbable-places-t
 oronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
