BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Summer Music: Prodigies & Power
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T213000
UID:blogto-235238@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/19/original_imagec81c4301-0345-40d6-888c-2ebcb6b7b6
 19.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Genius often reveals itself early — and boldly. Dohnányi’
 s Piano Quintet\, written at 17 and praised by Brahms\, brims with youthfu
 l ambition. Mendelssohn’s C minor Trio shows that same prodigious spirit
  transformed into sweeping Romantic authority. Prokofiev’s brilliant Son
 ata for Two Violins opens the night with sharp wit and kinetic drive. An e
 vening of fearless invention and blazing artistry.
LOCATION:Walter Hall
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-summer-music-prodigies-power-tor
 onto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ADNC Narrative Power Summit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260726T000000
UID:blogto-231284@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/02/23/original_imaged90fdfc6-f4e2-43e7-b581-0f35c6c3d2
 58.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The African Diaspora News Channel ADNC Narrative Power Summit 
 is a one-day\, high-impact gathering built to do one thing unapologeticall
 y: shift narrative power back into the hands of our communities.\nHeadlini
 ng the Summit is Phillip Scott\, Founder & CEO of African Diaspora News Ch
 annel (ADNC)\, a pioneering force in independent Black media and a leading
  advocate for media literacy\, narrative sovereignty\, and community accou
 ntability.\nUnder Phillip Scott’s leadership\, ADNC has become essential
  media infrastructure\, delivering coverage that challenges distorted narr
 atives and centers truth\, context\, and community power. His presence anc
 hors the Summit’s core message: Black media isn’t optional\, it’s es
 sential.\nThis landmark marquee event brings together Black media professi
 onals\, journalists\, artists\, activists\, policy thinkers\, and grassroo
 ts organizers from across the African Diaspora who understand one core rea
 lity: whoever controls the narrative controls the outcome\, politically\, 
 economically\, and culturally.\nAttendees will hear from international key
 note speakers from the United States\, alongside Toronto-based journalists
 \, cultural leaders\, and policy influencers who are actively shaping publ
 ic discourse. Through dynamic panels\, unfiltered conversations\, and prac
 tical\, real-world insights\, participants will gain tools to challenge ha
 rmful narratives\, counter misinformation\, and amplify voices that have h
 istorically been sidelined.\nBeyond the conversations\, the Summit is also
  a full experience. Guests will walk the Black Carpet Media Wall\, capture
  professional photos\, enjoy a delicious dinner and curated drinks\, live 
 music performance featuring Juno award winning artists\, Carlos Morgan and
  his band\, and special guest performances. Guests will also connect direc
 tly with the powerhouse ADNC team behind one of the most influential Black
 -owned media platforms today.\nIt’s equal parts strategy\, celebration\,
  and community\, because narrative power should feel as good as it is impa
 ctful.\nAt its core\, the ADNC Narrative Power Summit is about building na
 rrative muscle\, teaching communities how to consume media critically\, pr
 oduce content strategically\, and leverage storytelling as a vehicle for a
 ccountability\, advocacy\, and economic empowerment. This is action. It’
 s ownership.
LOCATION:Acqua Supper Club
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/adnc-narrative-power-summit-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ADNC Narrative Power Summit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T233000
UID:blogto-234293@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/28/original_image1fe43d8a-2888-47c2-885c-37ce025e8f
 d7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Produced by the African Diaspora News Channel (ADNC)\, in part
 nership with Emma Ansah of EA Public Relations\, this one-day\, high-impac
 t summit is unapologetically about ownership of our stories\, our voices\,
  and our influence. In a moment where misinformation\, distortion\, and er
 asure are constant\, this gathering is designed to equip Black communities
  with the tools to critically consume media\, strategically produce conten
 t\, and leverage storytelling for real-world impact.\nHeadlining the Summi
 t is Phillip Scott\, Founder & CEO of ADNC\, whose leadership has helped b
 uild one of the most influential independent Black-owned media platforms t
 oday. Under his direction\, ADNC has become essential media infrastructure
  centering truth\, accountability\, and community power in a media landsca
 pe that often does the opposite. His presence anchors the Summit’s core 
 message: Black media isn’t optional\, it’s essential.\nThis marquee ev
 ent brings together Black journalists\, media professionals\, artists\, ac
 tivists\, policy thinkers\, and grassroots organizers from across the Afri
 can Diaspora who understand a shared reality: whoever controls the narrati
 ve controls political\, economic\, and cultural outcomes.\nAttendees will 
 hear from international keynote speakers from the United States\, alongsid
 e Toronto-based journalists\, cultural leaders\, and policy influencers ac
 tively shaping public discourse. Through dynamic panels\, unfiltered conve
 rsations\, and practical insights\, participants will leave with actionabl
 e strategies to challenge harmful narratives\, counter misinformation\, an
 d amplify voices that have historically been sidelined.\nBeyond the conver
 sations\, the Summit is a full experience. Guests will walk the Black Carp
 et Media Wall\, capture professional photos\, enjoy a curated dinner and d
 rinks\, and experience live music performances featuring Juno Award–winn
 ing artist Carlos Morgan and his band\, along with special guest performan
 ces. Attendees will also have direct access to the ADNC team behind one of
  today’s most powerful Black-owned media platforms.\nEqual parts strateg
 y\, celebration\, and community\, the ADNC Narrative Power Summit is about
  building narrative muscle and reminding us that power feels good when it
 ’s finally in our hands
LOCATION:Acqua Supper Club
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/adnc-narrative-power-summit-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anga's Farm: An Afternoon in the Orchard - A Floral Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T160000
